{"archetypes":[{"name":"python-test-parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan lists python/test_config.py and python/test_ci_monitor.py for update but does not mention python/test_rebase.py, which has 20+ TierAttempt(\"cursor\", …) mocks and an explicit FIXER_TIER_ORDER assertion — all of which will break after the config.py tuple flip.","prompt_body":"Verify that every Python test file that asserts on FIXER_TIER_ORDER or embeds cursor/codex tier ordering in mock objects (TierAttempt, launch_calls, commit-message stubs) is listed in the plan's 'Files to modify/create' section. The plan currently names python/test_config.py and python/test_ci_monitor.py; check python/test_rebase.py and any other python/test_*.py file for cursor-first assertions that will break when python/config.py FIXER_TIER_ORDER flips to ('codex', 'cursor', 'claude'). For each unlisted file, identify the specific assertions that will fail and confirm whether the plan's 'make py-test (full suite)' note provides sufficient implementer guidance or whether the file must be added to the explicit change list. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"doc-sync-coverage","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan lists seven prose docs to sync but a targeted grep may surface additional cursor-first order references in docs not in the scope list (e.g. docs/workflow-lifecycle.md, docs/collaborative-sketches.md, skills/design references), plus the SKILL.md arrow-substring guard constraint is fragile and not verified against the exact proposed wording.","prompt_body":"Audit all documentation files in docs/, skills/, and scripts/*.md for residual 'Cursor → Codex' or 'cursor-first' order prose beyond the seven files the plan explicitly lists for update. Pay special attention to docs/workflow-lifecycle.md, docs/collaborative-sketches.md, and skills/design/references/brainstorm.md, which the plan labels as out-of-scope but may contain stale ordering text that creates drift. Also verify the SKILL.md arrow-substring guard: the plan says reword to use commas to avoid the literal 'Codex → Cursor → Claude' substring — check whether the proposed comma form ('Codex, then Cursor, then Claude — arrives at Claude') still accurately communicates the waterfall and whether test-implement-step2-routing.sh's assert_not_contains guard will pass with that exact phrasing. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
